pool.baseline:
hey, im still seeing access denied on that s3 bucket for the lambda. i thought the iam role had everything but i'm starting to think there's some kind of gatekeeper policy or something blocking us. 

i added this condition to the role just in case it's a source restriction issue, but it still fails:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::prod-app-logs-99/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:SourceVpc": "vpc-0a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

could there be something else acting like a gatekeeper that would just straight up deny the request even if the iam policy looks perfect? like some kind of hidden security layer that's just keeping us out?

